Advisory (radical innovation, do not apply here) — collapse the two parallelism dials into one core budget. Set `[testenv] commands = pytest -n {env:PYTEST_WORKERS:auto} {posargs}` and document the full matrix as `PYTEST_WORKERS=4 tox run-parallel`. One env then uses every core, four concurrent envs use a quarter each, and total worker count stays near the core count in both cases. No machine-specific number is baked into `tox.ini`, the posargs override still works, and each documented command gets one line. Offered for the operator to weigh against the cost of touching the plan again.

